[Music]  acclaimed chef and milk bar founder  that's christina tosi is out with a  playful new cookbook  aiming to inspire a new generation of  young bakers it's called  milk bar kids only is the fourth  cookbook from this acclaimed pastry chef  who is a two-time winner of the  prestigious james beard award  that recognizes culinary excellence and  she is  excellent with a capital e vladimir  dutier sat down with ms tosi and learned  how her baking  is about more than just satisfying your  sweet tooth vlad good morning to you  again i remember when she was here in  the studio she's awesome  she's amazing and there's an interesting  phenomena that developed  when the coronavirus pandemic but forced  much of the country  to stay at home gail people became  reacquainted with their ovens  right they bake for themselves they bake  for family and friends it wasn't just  toilet paper and sanitizing wipes that  sold out of stores  but flour and yeast as well baking had a  moment in 2020  and chef christina tozi was there to  meet it  half a cup of light brown sugar this is  what you're looking for it's smooth it's  creamy  no one's mad at it it looks very  delicious when the country went into  lockdown in the early days of the  pandemic  christina tozi headed to the kitchen we  need to take that cake we need to break  it down a little bit  the renowned chef met her fans in their  homes  hosting a bake club on instagram live  and boy did you all get after brittle  yesterday  you made pistachio brittle pecan brittle  butterscotch brittle  what did you learn i learned that  the power of being imperfectly perfect  is what i call it or comfortably human  perhaps  is is the most powerful tool i have  that community is a really powerful  thing the power of a baked good  is real and we need it now in the harder  times more than ever before  tozi has embraced that power for more  than a decade  in 2008 she opened milk bar a bakery  serving treats with a twist  like cereal milk ice cream there are now  13  milk bar outposts around the country  tozie has authored  four cookbooks including her latest milk  bar kids only  i wrote this book before this year so  it's kind of just ironic that  this book of celebration of looking  at the world through the lens of a kid  being a kid and getting in the kitchen  baking and being empowered by it they're  all such  meaningful things that we need right now  for anyone looking for the hide the  veggies in the cupcakes cookbook  this is unapologetically not it the way  that i was raised was always with  desserts as conduit  a platter of cookies is not about you  crushing the whole platter right  oh now you're telling me you've been  doing it wrong  no i believe that baked goods  are invitations into people's lives  they're opportunities to  share joy and heart and emotion  and it's about sharing as much as it is  about consuming  and little moments of things  are always going to be good for you so  one of the pro moves of this treat  is you put sprinkles on the bottom of  the pan for tozie the kitchen has always  been about connection do you ever notice  that people love  watching people cook or bake  i love when people come and hang out  with me in the kitchen  the kitchen is like my happy safe place  my grandma always welcomed me in  and it was kind of the place where we  talked about stuff  like i think you i get the most out of  people that just come and like hang out  and i'm like hey what's up how's your  day  what's going on anything good happen  what about the bad stuff you want to  talk about the bad stuff  it happens right here despite its  challenges  2020 has also brought opportunity for  the milk bar brand  most of its stores have reopened there's  been a jump in the online sales of its  care packages  over 340 000 have shipped and you can  now find milk bar confections in the  grocery aisles of target and whole foods  still tosi is determined to hang on to  the small business charm  i use my tummy as my guide when we're  testing new recipes  but i try to always use my heart as my  guide everywhere else  even when making the biggest heaviest  business decisions  because at the end of the day milk bar  is an extension of me milk bar is an  extension of the people  that i work with and we're all humans  just trying to figure out how to show up  in the world  my tummy is my guide too even as it  expands josie  also listens to her roughly 200  employees after this summer's  nationwide cry for social justice  milkbar updated several of its policies  tosi's team members now have an  additional  paid time off for mental health and to  vote in the upcoming election  how about that yeah she's awesome yeah  she is awesome  she's right the power of baked goods is  real because i'm still trying to  counteract that power  from back in april and may when i was i  wrote that down too anthony  and i like what she said imperfectly  perfect and comfortably human  life is uncertain i always eat dessert  first  that was that was a magnet on my fridge  when i was a kid my mom had it up there  i still live by it yeah  it's amazing what i found it's amazing  what power a cinnamon bun can have  that's right  pandemic thank you vlad

